title: ESBCACHE Kernel EA Bypass — Unsigned Driver Load Attempt
id: a8c2d3e4-f5b6-7890-cdef-123456789abc
status: experimental
description: >
  Detects behavioral indicators of the $Kernel.Purge.ESBCache EA injection bypass
  for loading unsigned kernel drivers on Windows 11 24H2.
  The bypass involves injecting a forged ESBCache EA (flags=0x20) directly into
  the NTFS MFT of a .sys file offline, causing CipVerifyFileCache (ci.dll) to
  return STATUS_SUCCESS before any Authenticode validation.
author: Research
date: 2026-06-04
references:
  - lab/poc/b1-file-hash-ffi/cipverifyfilecache_full_analysis.md
  - ci.dll 26100.8328 CipVerifyFileCache @ 0x180093028
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.T1553.006
  - attack.T1014

---
# Rule 1: Unsigned driver loaded from non-system path (sc create/start pattern)
title: Kernel Driver Service Created from Non-Standard Path
id: b9d3e4f5-a6c7-8901-defa-234567890bcd
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: sysmon
detection:
  selection_registry:
    EventID: 13
    TargetObject|contains: '\CurrentControlSet\Services\'
    Details|contains: '.sys'
  filter_system_drivers:
    TargetObject|contains:
      - '\SystemRoot\System32\drivers\'
      - '\SystemRoot\SysWow64\'
      - 'C:\Windows\System32\drivers\'
  condition: selection_registry and not filter_system_drivers
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate driver installers placing drivers in custom directories
level: medium

---
# Rule 2: Service start for a driver not in System32\drivers
title: Kernel Driver Loaded from User-Accessible Path
id: c4e5f6a7-b8d9-0123-efab-345678901cde
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: sysmon
detection:
  selection:
    EventID: 6   # Sysmon: DriverLoaded
    ImageLoaded|re: '^(?!C:\\Windows\\(System32|SysWow64)\\).+\.sys$'
  condition: selection
falsepositives:
  - Development environments
  - Antivirus/EDR drivers in custom paths
level: high

---
# Rule 3: esbtest.sys proof-of-concept specific
title: ESBCACHE Bypass PoC Driver Loaded (esbtest.sys)
id: d5f6a7b8-c9e0-1234-fabc-456789012def
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: sysmon
detection:
  selection:
    EventID: 6
    ImageLoaded|contains: 'esbtest'
  condition: selection
falsepositives:
  - None (research artifact)
level: critical

---
# Rule 4: ESBCacheBypass registry key written (esbtest DriverEntry ran)
title: ESBCACHE Bypass Registry Marker Written
id: e6a7b8c9-d0f1-2345-abcd-567890123ef0
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: sysmon
detection:
  selection:
    EventID: 13
    TargetObject|contains: 'SOFTWARE\ESBCacheBypass'
  condition: selection
falsepositives:
  - None (research-specific key)
level: critical

---
# Rule 5: CodeIntegrity Event 3089 (catalog hit for driver) — normal but useful for baseline
title: CodeIntegrity Driver Load via Catalog Cache Hit
id: f7b8c9d0-e1f2-3456-bcde-678901234f01
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: 'Microsoft-Windows-CodeIntegrity/Operational'
detection:
  selection:
    EventID: 3089   # Signature check complete, catalog source
  condition: selection
falsepositives:
  - All legitimate catalog-signed driver loads
level: informational
